{"type":"text","timestamp":1794229992043,"sessionID":"ses_e3f910ca4ffeeW0K0w1qsifGet","part":{"id":"prt_1c070487c001PkPH5Enyw91TxQ","sessionID":"ses_e3f910ca4ffeeW0K0w1qsifGet","messageID":"msg_1c06f44d9001fFODMvBE0XAdxn","type":"text","text":"To effectively use the provided tools, here's a structured guide based on their categories and functionalities:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Azure DevOps Tools**\n**Use case:** Managing Azure DevOps projects, pull requests, work items, and server info.\n\n- **`get_my_pull_requests`**  \n  *Purpose:* Fetch pull requests created by the current user.  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `status` (optional): Filter by status (`active`, `completed`, `abandoned`, or `all`).  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.azure.get_my_pull_requests({ status: \"active\" });\n  ```\n\n- **`get_work_item_history`**  \n  *Purpose:* Retrieve revision history for a specific work item.  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `workItemId` (required): The ID of the work item.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.azure.get_work_item_history({ workItemId: 123 });\n  ```\n\n- **`get_server_info`**  \n  *Purpose:* Get server version, build info, and connectivity status.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.azure.get_server_info();\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### **2. OpenCode Tools**\n**Use case:** Managing MCP resources, models, sessions, and worktrees.\n\n- **`models`**  \n  *Purpose:* Search for available models (e.g., chat, image).  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `query`: Search term for model names/IDs.  \n  - `provider`: Filter by provider (e.g., \"openai\").  \n  - `type`: Model type (`chat` or `image`).  \n  - `all`: Include older versions.  \n  - `limit`/`offset`: Pagination.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.opencode.models({ type: \"chat\", limit: 10 });\n  ```\n\n- **`list_mcp_resources`**  \n  *Purpose:* List documents/records from MCP servers.  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `server` (optional): Filter by server name.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.opencode.list_mcp_resources({ server: \"my-server\" });\n  ```\n\n- **`worktree_create`**  \n  *Purpose:* Create a named worktree.  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `name`: Worktree name.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.opencode.worktree_create({ name: \"feature-branch\" });\n  ```\n\n- **`worktree_remove`**  \n  *Purpose:* Remove a worktree (use `force` for forced removal).  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `directory`: Absolute path of the worktree.  \n  - `force` (optional): Discard changes.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.opencode.worktree_remove({ directory: \"/path/to/worktree\", force: true });\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### **3. Roslyn Tools**\n**Use case:** Code analysis and project dependency management.\n\n- **`find_async_violations`**  \n  *Purpose:* Detect async/await misuse (e.g., `.Result`, `.Wait()`).  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.roslyn.find_async_violations();\n  ```\n\n- **`get_project_dependencies`**  \n  *Purpose:* List project dependencies (direct and transitive).  \n  *Parameters:*  \n  - `project`: Project name or `.csproj` filename.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.roslyn.get_project_dependencies({ project: \"MyProject.csproj\" });\n  ```\n\n- **`get_public_api_surface`**  \n  *Purpose:* Enumerate all public/protected types and members in a solution.  \n  *Example:*  \n  ```javascript\n  await tools.roslyn.get_public_api_surface();\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### **Key Tips**\n- **Pagination:** Use `limit` and `offset` for large datasets (e.g., `models`, `search`).  \n- **Contextual Parameters:** Some tools require specific context (e.g., Azure project names, server IDs).  \n- **Forced Actions:** Use `force` sparingly (e.g., `worktree_remove`).  \n- **Model Selection:** Prioritize \"chat\" models for tool-calling; \"image\" models are for generation tasks.  \n\nLet me know your specific use case, and I can tailor the tool usage!","time":{"start":1794229946492,"end":1794229992043}}}
